beh('B-append','A1','Follower RPC handler, usually main loop; empty fast heartbeat may be concurrent','Request term, previous-log identity, local log/snapshot and configuration','AppendEntries dispatch',['s-append','s-rpc-dispatch','s-heartbeat-dispatch'],implementation_guards=['Rejects old term and mismatching previous-log term/index; newer term makes follower; ordinary same-term append also makes nonfollower step down except transfer candidate.'],durable_effects=['Conflicting suffix is deleted; duplicate same-term entries skipped; new entries persisted before success.'],writes=['Leader identity, cached last log, latest/committed configuration, local commit index, last contact'],important_branches=['Commit advancement uses min(LeaderCommitIndex, local getLastIndex), not explicitly the last index checked by this request.','Truncating an uncommitted configuration restores the committed configuration before processing replacement entries.','Empty heartbeat fast path has previous index/term zero, no entries and commit index zero, so it cannot itself commit logs.'],external_effects=['processLogs enqueues newly considered committed entries before successful reply.'],cross_activity_effects={'A2':'Term/role and known-leader updates establish current request context.','A4':'Log conflict and received configuration entries alter participant eligibility.','A5':'Follower commitment directly drives FSM delivery.'},unknowns=['Whether a legal request can advertise a commit frontier beyond its checked prefix while a divergent local suffix remains; producer/backtracking and snapshot histories must be composed before alleging unsafe application.'])
