entries={
'A1':('Form and propagate committed log decisions','Leader storage and replication reports feed a voter-only commitment tracker; current-term threshold admits commit advancement; followers accept leader commit positions after prefix checks.',['Raft.dispatchLogs','commitment.recalculate','Raft.appendEntries'],['s-dispatch','s-commitment','s-append']),
'A2':('Acquire and maintain authority in an eligible context','Term-persistent elections use voter membership and log freshness; leader lifetimes isolate support and pending work. VerifyLeader and lease are distinct authority consumers.',['Raft.runCandidate','Raft.requestVote','Raft.runLeader','Raft.verifyLeader','Raft.checkLeaderLease'],['s-candidate','s-vote','s-leader-setup','s-verify-register','s-lease']),
'A3':('Recover eligible participation','Constructor and follower snapshot installation reconstruct state; replication backs up or installs snapshots; explicit user restore is a separate caller-authorized replacement.',['NewRaft','Raft.installSnapshot','Raft.restoreUserSnapshot'],['s-recovery','s-install','s-user-restore']),
'A4':('Control participant eligibility','Latest logged configuration controls voting and commitment immediately; committed configuration is retained for rollback and snapshots; all peers, including nonvoters, replicate.',['nextConfiguration','Raft.appendConfigurationEntry','Raft.startStopReplication'],['s-config-change','s-config-append','s-repl-membership']),
'A5':('Consume decisions in the application FSM','Dedicated FSM goroutine serializes Apply, configuration callbacks, barriers and restore. Enqueue position differs from completed application.',['Raft.processLogs','Raft.runFSM'],['s-apply','s-fsm']),
'A6':('Preserve and reconstruct protocol history','Injected durable log/stable/snapshot interfaces hold terms, votes and history. Library coordinates writes, compaction, and startup replay; in-repository stores remain implementation surfaces.',['Raft.persistVote','Raft.takeSnapshot','LogStore','StableStore'],['s-election','s-snapshot','s-store','s-stable']),
'A7':('Define invocation and observed completion','Client futures report asynchronously; Apply completion is tied to FSM response, loss of leadership can leave write outcome ambiguous, and VerifyLeader claims protection against stale reads.',['Raft.Apply','Raft.Barrier','Raft.VerifyLeader','Future.Error'],['s-client-api','s-verify-api','s-future-contract'])}
for i,(p,r,e,s) in entries.items():activities.append(dict(class_id=i,applicability='applicable',purpose=p,realization_summary=r,entry_points=e,source_ids=s))
formation='Apply admission reaches the leader main loop, which assigns term/index and stores logs before reporting self support. Per-peer replication sends bounded batches with previous index/term, retries rejected prefixes and falls back to snapshots for missing history. Follower append persists nonduplicate entries before success. The leader-lifetime commitment tracker counts only current voters, advances at a majority index only after the first entry of this term is supported, and notifies the main loop. That loop advances commit/configuration state and enqueues committed tuples for runFSM; FSM application supplies command responses. Replication CommitTimeout carries the leader commit frontier to idle followers; their processLogs path feeds the same serialized FSM consumer.'
context='A follower without recent contact campaigns only if it is a voter. Per-attempt pre-vote/election channels isolate replies; real elections persist term and vote, and remote handlers enforce term, candidate eligibility, prior vote and log freshness. A winning majority creates a fresh leader commitment/replication lifetime and appends a current-term noop. Newer-term RPCs, replication rejection signals, voter-only lease loss or committed local removal can end leadership. Cleanup stops old workers and rejects pending futures; surviving old replies refer to old tracker/channel objects. Already enqueued FSM work has its own owner and may complete after stepdown. Persistent logs/snapshots and vote freshness carry prior decided history into later campaigns; new leaders collect fresh replication support.'
connection='The authority context selects both the log that may be advanced and the eligible voters whose support can advance it. Membership is logged, normally one uncommitted change at a time, and updates the commitment voter set and replication workers immediately; followers roll back latest membership with a conflicting suffix. Elections compare retained log/snapshot history, while the current-term commitment threshold prevents using mere old-term support as fresh authority. Recovery reconstructs history and configuration before campaigning. Heartbeats confirm contact but carry no commit index; VerifyLeader consumes separate per-request callbacks and lease checks count recent voter contacts. Verification registration includes nonvoter replication workers despite a voter-derived threshold, retained as an unresolved eligibility question rather than a guarantee.'
m=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured HashiCorp Raft Go module: leader/follower protocol loops, replication, configuration, persistence coordination, snapshots and FSM/future APIs. Caller implements FSM and may inject stores/transports; in-repository implementations remain in scope and are not externalized merely by injection.',protocol_contexts=['Term and leader lifetime','Latest and committed membership','Per-peer replication stream','Log/snapshot index and term','Per-client future'],external_interfaces=['FSM','LogStore','StableStore','SnapshotStore','Transport','Apply/Barrier/VerifyLeader and configuration APIs'],ownership=['Main loop owns configurations and leaderState; heartbeat fast path is an explicit concurrent exception for empty requests.','Replication workers own progress with specific locks/atomics; commitment has its own mutex; FSM and snapshot work use separate goroutines.'],selection_injection=['Client-selected stores, FSM and transport','Config timeouts, MaxAppendEntries, protocol version, pre-vote and snapshot settings'],variants=['Normal and pipeline replication','Voters and nonvoters','Snapshot recovery and explicit user restore','Legacy protocol/snapshot compatibility paths read only at backbone level'],source_ids=['s-recovery','s-transport','s-fsm','s-store','s-config-contract','s-heartbeat-dispatch'],unknowns=['Full transport pipeline/error behavior and built-in store failure semantics remain unread.']),activities=activities,behaviors=B,facts=F,core_overview=dict(status='usable',formation=dict(explanation=formation,behavior_ids=['B-dispatch','B-replicate','B-commitment','B-leader-consume','B-append','B-fsm'],fact_ids=['F-match','F-commit-frontier'],source_ids=['s-dispatch','s-replication','s-commitment','s-leader-loop','s-append','s-fsm']),context=dict(explanation=context,behavior_ids=['B-election','B-leader-lifetime','B-lease','B-recovery'],source_ids=['s-follower','s-candidate','s-election','s-vote','s-leader-setup','s-lease','s-recovery']),connection=dict(explanation=connection,behavior_ids=['B-configuration','B-leader-lifetime','B-recovery','B-verify-admit','B-verify-notify','B-verify-complete'],fact_ids=['F-match','F-commit-frontier','F-verify-tally'],source_ids=['s-config-append','s-repl-membership','s-commitment','s-append','s-recovery','s-verify-register','s-verify-future']),open_details=['Verification acknowledgment eligibility with nonvoters and independent lease timing.','Follower commit bound versus request-checked prefix under recovery/backtracking histories.','Storage failures between separate vote-key updates; pipeline error and peer-address transition details.'],core_gaps=[],rationale='Representative formation and context lifecycles, their producers/consumers and necessary membership/recovery/completion paths are traced. Usable navigation does not mean exhaustive coverage or correctness.'),surfaces=[dict(entry_point='Raft.appendEntries commit-index calculation',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-append'],reason='Local log end can exceed request-checked prefix. Need a legal producer/recovery history preserving a conflicting suffix before considering an obligation.',source_ids=['s-append','s-repl-input','s-install'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='Raft.persistVote separate StableStore writes',disposition='deferred',reason='Vote term and candidate persist separately, and error handling denies the current vote. Crash/error recovery semantics and subsequent candidate interpretation require investigation.',source_ids=['s-election','s-vote','s-stable'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='NetworkTransport pipeline and built-in stores',disposition='deferred',reason='Interfaces and heartbeat routing read; full pipeline error/close ownership and in-memory/file persistence implementation remain to be traced.',source_ids=['s-transport','s-heartbeat-dispatch','s-store'],high_consequence=True)])
q=dict(question='Can VerifyLeader consume affirmative acknowledgments from Nonvoter replication workers as the voter majority needed to confirm current leadership, and can that produce successful verification without eligible authority support under a legal history?',importance='A false positive in the documented stale-read protection can expose stale FSM state after a voter majority has moved to another leader; local acknowledgment eligibility is the first discriminator, not yet an observed cluster consequence.',source_ids=['s-verify-api','s-verify-register','s-verify-future','s-repl-notify','s-heartbeat','s-repl-membership','s-config-contract','s-leader-loop','s-lease'],participants=['Local leader voter','Other configured voters','Configured Nonvoter replica'],objects=['verifyFuture','followerReplication.notify','latest Configuration'],contexts=['Stable mixed voter/nonvoter configuration','One leader lifetime and one verification invocation','Voter contact unavailable while nonvoter replies remain possible'],event_paths=['VerifyLeader -> leaderLoop -> verifyLeader -> per-peer notify registration','heartbeat/append success -> notifyAll -> verifyFuture.vote -> leaderLoop verification completion'],activity_classes=['A2'],behavior_ids=['B-verify-admit','B-verify-notify','B-verify-complete'],fact_ids=['F-verify-tally'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-configuration':'Establishes suffrage and creates replication workers for both voters and nonvoters.','B-lease':'Independent voter-only contact timer may end leadership; must preserve its ordering rather than assume it cannot run.','B-election':'Supplies legal acquisition/loss history if demonstrating an actual obsolete leader rather than only local eligibility.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['commitment.recalculate and checkLeaderLease explicitly restrict support to voters; this is not evidence that those paths have the same discrepancy.','Leader cleanup fails pending verification and nonleader admission rejects requests.','A negative callback or higher-term RPC can prevent success; a legal check must control actual message scheduling rather than inject contradictory replies.','API promises leader verification but does not explicitly spell out per-request voter accounting; applicability must be derived from the actual authority mechanism and source contract.'],unknowns=['Determine whether the scoped responsibility should be expressed as eligible acknowledgment accounting or as stale-leader verification, without treating an arbitrary disconnected leader as already obsolete.','Construct a legal prefix and reply schedule that preserves the independent lease/stepdown paths while distinguishing a nonvoter callback from an eligible voter acknowledgment.'],priority=3,trigger_rationale='Source discrepancy is direct: voter-only quorumSize, all-peer verification registration, identity-free callback tally, and nil completion at threshold. Contract reading and a small local callback experiment can distinguish eligibility before a costly full partition test; the follower prefix lead requires substantially more legal-history reconstruction.',disposition='concrete_suspicion',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')
